{"title":"1977 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/5/5753734e29398cf1e59cb67a78e86180c7499f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d,e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> are positive numbers bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, i.e, if they lie in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7db0d1c44b17ab521242db4599465126d5ad617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[p,q], 0 &lt; p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d42a948da6239cf2d21f08336d9b2ad4f8a65b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b +c +d +e)\\left(\\frac{1}{a} +\\frac {1}{b} +\\frac{1}{c} + \\frac{1}{d} +\\frac{1}{e}\\right) \\le 25 + 6\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac {p}{q}} - \\sqrt {\\frac{q}{p}}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"481\" height=\"47\" />\nand determine when there is equality.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fix four of the variables and allow the other to vary. Suppose, for example, we fix all but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Then the expression on the LHS has the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/8/288469c86db4819032697e66684daed1fe003e41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r + x)(s + \\frac{1}{x}) = (rs + 1) + sx + \\frac{r}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"277\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are fixed. But this is convex. That is to say, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> increases if first decreases, then increases. So its maximum must occur at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19a8531373871b279fc778aa78a17f0f88015206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cbaaaf7325316b0c6ee519f1d7246c9150d743a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />. This is true for each variable.\n</p><p>Suppose all five are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or all five are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then the LHS is 25, so the inequality is true and strict unless <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f149595b4c16eb76ff9d263f681aadc7322a0ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />. If four are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and one is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then the LHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/034b58f6ff4994b4b758c56065c81491104c8209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 4\\left(\\frac{p}{q} + \\frac{q}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"123\" height=\"43\" />. Similarly if four are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and one is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. If three are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and two are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then the LHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92a6f03033f925648f3e74e8dc0b755cf8a7b0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 + 6\\left(\\frac{p}{q} + \\frac{q}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"123\" height=\"43\" />. Similarly if three are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and two are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/9854130260a0e2b74548ab7fc805f55acf2f958c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q} + \\frac{q}{p} \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"81\" height=\"36\" /> with equality iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f149595b4c16eb76ff9d263f681aadc7322a0ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />, so if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e4542d00da66a56639f43c4ac48682d73eeb0b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &lt; q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, then three of one and two of the other gives a larger LHS than four of one and one of the other. Finally, we note that the RHS is in fact <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92a6f03033f925648f3e74e8dc0b755cf8a7b0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 + 6\\left(\\frac{p}{q} + \\frac{q}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"123\" height=\"43\" />, so the inequality is true with equality iff either (1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f149595b4c16eb76ff9d263f681aadc7322a0ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> or (2) three of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c711f0150c30098d59f3b9b87b42d1211443569c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v, w, x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"11\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and two are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or vice versa.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO\" title=\"1977 USAMO\">1977 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1977 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1977\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1977 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1977 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1977 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1977 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1977 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172617\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 204/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1237/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6065/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.821      1 -total\n 56.56%    6.686      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 40.92%    4.837      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11371:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172617 and revision id 95653. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}